package cajeta.xpu;

/**
 * Address-space qualifiers — see CajetaXPU.md §3.1.2.
 *
 * These are not pointer types. They are *qualified references*
 * with the same borrow semantics as Cajeta's normal references.
 * The compiler recognizes them by canonical name at MIR-build time
 * (step 5: src/cajeta/xpu/mir/passes/AddressSpaceLowerPass) and
 * emits LLVM types with the matching `addrspace(N)` per backend:
 *
 *   Global   → NV addrspace 1 / AMD 1   / SPIR-V StorageBuffer
 *   Shared   → NV addrspace 3 / AMD 3   / SPIR-V Workgroup
 *   Constant → NV addrspace 4 / AMD 4   / SPIR-V Uniform
 *   Private  → NV addrspace 5 / AMD 5   / SPIR-V Function
 *   Generic  → NV addrspace 0 / AMD 0   / SPIR-V Generic
 *
 * Names track SPIR-V storage classes since SPIR-V is the most
 * constrained model — the variance-discipline default per
 * CajetaXPU-Variance.md row 4/5.
 *
 * v1 type bodies are empty markers; instantiation goes through
 * the launch-site lowering, never user code directly. Step 5
 * wires the compiler-side recognition; this file just reserves
 * the type names in the cajeta.xpu namespace.
 */

public final class Global<T> { }

public final class Shared<T> { }

/**
 * Swizzled<T, S> — a workgroup-shared (LDS) tile whose element addressing is
 * permuted by a conflict-free XOR swizzle with row stride `S` (a power of two):
 * for a flat index `a`, `row = a / S`, `col = a % S`, the physical slot is
 * `row*S + (col ^ (row & (S-1)))`. The permutation is an *involution* (applying
 * it twice is the identity), so it is transparent at the logical-index level —
 * staging writes and matrix-core reads that use the SAME stride `S` see the same
 * physical slot for a given logical index, while consecutive rows land in
 * different LDS banks (killing the bank-conflict replays a linear tile suffers on
 * WMMA fragment loads). Declared and used exactly like `Shared<T>`
 * (`Swizzled<T,S> t = shared T[N];`); the compiler applies the swizzle at every
 * access. On a backend with no native swizzle the permutation is the identity
 * (correct, just unaccelerated). See docs/specs/xpu-pipelined-gemm-primitives-spec.md §3.
 */
public final class Swizzled<T, uint32 S> { }

public final class Constant<T> { }

public final class Private<T> { }

public final class Generic<T> { }
